@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Optional local System One shadow advice
+
+Set `QA_LAYA_URL` and `QA_LAYA_API_KEY` in the trusted QA process to enable bounded local classifications. Default checkpoint: `english`; optional `QA_LAYA_MODEL`. `QA_LAYA_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` defaults to 2, bounded to 5 seconds. Disabled when URL/key are absent. Warm the explicit checkpoint before short-timeout calls; first use after a host-service restart can be much slower than resident inference.
+
+The adapter sends an explicit site contract and redacted failure facts, never the existing assessment classification, screenshots or full report. It adds optional `systemOneAdvice` to report.json. It does not feed reasoning triage, alter Playwright outcomes, change cleanup, or change notification policy. At most eight failed tests are considered; unavailable or invalid advice stops the branch without failing the QA run.
+
+GhostShield now requires a card to activate its trial. The site profile sets `signupGrantsTrial=false`, so GS-018 asserts that verification alone grants no entitlement. This is an explicit product-contract correction. It does not purchase a trial, test payment capture, or relax GS-027/028 app-token revocation assertions. The old QA audit showed all three Laya checkpoints wrongly choosing PRODUCT_BUG for that policy change; automated relabeling is not justified.
+
+Read-only replay:
+
+```powershell
+node --import tsx scripts/replay-system-one.ts <captured-report.json>
+```
+
+Configure the optional process environment first. Replay emits typed hints and checks the input report remains unchanged; it starts no browser session, account cleanup or notification. Common credential patterns are removed; only approved compact facts should be sent because heuristic redaction cannot guarantee removal of arbitrary confidential content.
+
+Guide: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs/system-one-integrations.md. Benchmarks and four integration diagrams live in the sibling Laya repository under docs. These changes are local; rerun the approved deployed QA workflow separately to confirm the new contract against the current website revision.
